{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to require passwords of at least 12 characters and three character classes. The policy persisted through a verified node restart, with AlmaLinux 9.6 and the existing 5.14 kernel unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created /etc/security/pwquality.conf.d/99-password-complexity.conf with minlen=12 and minclass=3.","Verified that PAM consumes libpwquality through system-auth and password-auth.","Confirmed effective enforcement: short and insufficient-class samples were rejected, while a compliant generated sample was accepted.","Safely restarted node1 and verified its changed boot identity, recovered system health, active SSH service, unchanged policy checksum, and post-restart enforcement."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"New passwords must be at least 12 characters","command_ids":["cmd-89108cfdb40940f0","cmd-31819dc0641046cf","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"],"summary":"The policy contains minlen=12; before and after restart, pwscore rejected an 11-character sample specifically for being shorter than 12 characters."},{"requirement":"New passwords must use at least three character classes","command_ids":["cmd-89108cfdb40940f0","cmd-31819dc0641046cf","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"],"summary":"The policy contains minclass=3; before and after restart, pwscore rejected a 12-character one-class sample and accepted a generated long four-class sample."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software","command_ids":["cmd-d503e7c768f4457b","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"],"summary":"The existing AlmaLinux 9.6, kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6, PAM, and libpwquality stack were retained; the same release and kernel remained after restart."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ee06f52198f849c0","cmd-0f4eda3e663a49b8","cmd-d7323d3d70a94b1f","cmd-935b30a35d074caf","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID 717db5a2-895d-4bfb-b8a8-d4891c7b7b01 showed a running system, active SSH, zero failed units, and the policy checksum. The reboot was acknowledged and disconnected the session. The recovered node reports changed boot ID 6a44e7d6-860b-4772-9f29-ba53daf2d4b1, running state, active SSH, zero failed units, identical policy checksum, and successful policy enforcement."}]}
